### Re: Purchase of 14 Oakfield Road, Galway

Dear Ms Byrne,

Thank you for instructing us to act on your proposed purchase of **14 Oakfield Road, Galway** (“the Property”). This letter sets out the basis on which we will act for you and the terms of our engagement.

## 1. Scope of our work

Our work will ordinarily include:

1. taking your instructions and advising you on the conveyancing process;
2. obtaining and reviewing the contract for sale and title documentation;
3. raising and reviewing pre-contract enquiries;
4. advising you on the legal title to the Property and the principal terms of the contract;
5. negotiating appropriate amendments to the contract, where required;
6. reviewing available planning documentation and certificates of compliance from a legal perspective;
7. liaising with the vendor’s solicitor, your lender, auctioneer and other relevant parties;
8. arranging execution of the contract and payment of the deposit;
9. carrying out standard pre-closing searches;
10. preparing for and completing the purchase;
11. preparing and submitting the stamp duty return, based on information supplied by you, and arranging payment of stamp duty from funds provided by you;
12. submitting the transfer and any related documents for registration with Tailte Éireann; and
13. reporting to you following completion and, where applicable, providing title documentation to your lender.

If you are obtaining mortgage finance, we will also act for your lender where permitted and where the lender appoints us. Any unusual or additional lender requirements may result in an additional fee, which we will discuss with you in advance.

## 2. Work not included

Unless separately agreed in writing, our work does not include:

- a structural survey, valuation, engineering inspection or environmental assessment;
- verification of boundaries, measurements, physical condition or services;
- technical advice on planning permission, building regulations, fire safety, defects or certificates of compliance;
- tax, financial or investment advice, other than the ordinary conveyancing aspects of stamp duty;
- advice concerning the contents of the Property;
- litigation or dispute resolution;
- rectification of title defects, boundary disputes or other exceptional title issues;
- negotiation of a co-ownership agreement, declaration of trust or separate family-law advice; or
- advice on letting, development, commercial use or future alterations to the Property.

You should arrange an independent survey by a suitably qualified engineer or surveyor before becoming contractually bound.

## 3. Professional fee, VAT and outlays

Our fixed professional fee for a standard residential purchase is:

| Description | Amount |
|---|---:|
| Professional fee | €1,200.00 |
| VAT at the applicable rate (currently 23%) | €276.00 |
| Total fee including VAT | €1,476.00 |
| Outlays | Additional |

Outlays are payments made to third parties on your behalf and may include:

- Tailte Éireann registration fees;
- Registry of Deeds fees, if applicable;
- search fees;
- law searcher or closing agent fees;
- Companies Registration Office searches, where relevant;
- stamp duty;
- commissioner for oaths or notarial fees;
- bank transfer and courier charges; and
- other necessary third-party expenses.

Stamp duty and registration fees depend on the purchase price, title and circumstances of the transaction. We will provide details once the relevant information is available. You must place us in cleared funds for all fees, VAT, outlays, stamp duty, the balance purchase price and any other sums required before completion.

The fixed fee assumes a routine transaction completed within a reasonable period and without unusual complexity. If additional work becomes necessary—for example, because of a title defect, planning issue, boundary problem, delayed completion, bridging finance, multiple loan facilities or substantial renegotiation—we will notify you before carrying out chargeable additional work and provide an updated estimate or agree a further fee.

This letter, together with any accompanying costs notice, is intended to provide the information required under **section 150 of the Legal Services Regulation Act 2015**.

## 4. Your responsibilities

You agree to:

- provide complete, accurate and timely instructions and documentation;
- inform us immediately of any change in your circumstances, contact details, funding arrangements or intended use of the Property;
- read all documents and advice sent to you and raise any questions promptly;
- arrange a survey and any specialist inspections you consider appropriate;
- ensure that mortgage approval and all lender conditions are satisfied;
- provide cleared funds when requested; and
- not commit to a completion date, removal arrangements or expenditure until we confirm that it is safe to do so.

You should not sign a contract, pay a non-refundable deposit or take possession of the Property without first obtaining our advice.

## 5. Identity, anti-money laundering and source of funds

We are required by law to verify your identity and address and to obtain information concerning the source of the funds and wealth used for the purchase. You must provide all documents and explanations reasonably requested by us.

We may carry out electronic identity checks and retain copies of identification documents. We may be unable to act, or may be required to cease acting, if satisfactory documentation is not provided. Applicable law may also require us to make reports to relevant authorities without informing you.

Purchase funds should generally come from a bank account in your name. We will not accept cash or third-party funds without prior approval and satisfactory supporting documentation.

## 6. Mortgage finance

Any loan approval is subject to the lender’s conditions and does not constitute an unconditional commitment to lend. You remain responsible for ensuring that finance is available before signing an unconditional contract.

Where we also act for your lender, we owe duties to both you and the lender. We may be required to disclose relevant information to the lender, including issues affecting title, value, planning, occupancy or your contribution to the purchase price. If a conflict arises, we may be unable to continue acting for one or both parties.

## 7. Communications and payment security

We may communicate with you by post, telephone, email and secure electronic systems using the contact details you provide. Email is not completely secure, and you accept the ordinary risks associated with electronic communications.

**Fraud warning:** Our client-account bank details will not change during the transaction. You must verify any payment details directly with us by telephone using a previously verified number before transferring funds. We will not be responsible for payments made to an incorrect account where our payment-verification instructions have not been followed.

## 8. Client funds

Money received on your behalf will be held in our client account in accordance with applicable solicitors’ accounts regulations. Any entitlement to interest will be governed by our client-account policy and applicable professional rules.

We may deduct our agreed fees, VAT and outlays from funds held for you after providing you with a bill of costs or other appropriate notification.

## 9. Confidentiality and data protection

We will keep your information confidential, subject to legal and professional obligations. We may disclose information where necessary to progress the transaction, including to the vendor’s solicitor, your lender, Tailte Éireann, the Revenue Commissioners, search agents and other professional advisers or service providers.

We will process personal data in accordance with applicable data-protection law and our privacy notice, a copy of which is available at [website/provided separately].

## 10. Conflicts of interest

You must tell us if you become aware of any actual or potential conflict of interest. If a conflict arises that cannot properly be managed, we may be required to cease acting.

## 11. Timing

Any proposed timeframe is an estimate only. Completion depends on matters outside our control, including receipt of satisfactory title documents, replies to enquiries, mortgage funds, searches and cooperation from third parties. We cannot guarantee a particular completion date unless and until it has been formally agreed by the parties.

